title: Counter real-path — dread rises each turn, gates death, survives
  save/restore
story: counter-demo
description: ADR-264 real-path through the bundle. A `define counter dread`
  rises 20/turn (`raise dread by 20` in an `on every turn` clause), a
  comparison gates death (`kill the player when dread is at least 100`), and
  the counter value survives a save/restore. Proves declaration + mutation +
  condition read end to end.

---

# dread: 20, then 40 over two turns.
> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

# Save at dread 40, then push on — dread 60, 80.
$save vigil

> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

# Restore: dread is back to 40 (the save persisted the counter value).
$restore vigil

# From 40: three more turns reach 60, 80, 100 → `is at least 100` kills.
> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

> wait
[EVENT: true, type="if.event.player.died"]
